  "source": {
    "kind": "probed",
    "captured_at": "2026-10-17",
    "description": "Ordered ecp-2 WebSocket frames retained from a live probe of the Streaming Stick 4K of roku-streaming-stick-4k-3820eu2-15-3-4, ECP network access Enabled, taken to learn which authenticate frames the set accepts. Each exchange is its own session. The challenge is a fixed nonce with its answer recomputed, and the uptime is a same-shape value. Frames the set answered by dropping the connection without a reply (an authenticate whose request-id is a number or is missing) have no frame to keep and are stated as a claim instead. The request-events exchanges ran on an authenticated session; the subscription list is the one the Roku mobile app for Android sends. The launch and input exchanges ran on an authenticated session with YouTube (837) and Netflix (12) installed; ws.launch and the foreground exchanges were sent while 837 ran (with params it restarted, without them it was left alone); ws.input was sent from the home screen and launched 837. The params are the keys the Roku mobile app sends, with an all-zero session id."
  },
